  "body": "## What changed\n\nReported in #195: \"the origin is drawn approx 1px wide, with small text. Z isn't visible against the background. It should be drawn chunkier and shorter.\"\n\n- The origin triads are 1 px GPU overlay lines (a wgpu line has no width). They are now **also stroked in screen space** by the egui painter - 3 px axis colour over a 5 px dark outline - via a new `interact::gizmo_segments`, projected with the same camera math as the labels. The GPU lines stay (the overlay's line-count laws and picking read them).\n- **Shorter:** 15% of the model extent with an 8 mm floor (was 25% / 10 mm).\n- **Readable Z:** a brighter blue (0.38, 0.64, 1.0); world-axis dimming 0.8 (was 0.55 for lines, 0.65 for letters).\n- **Axis letters** 1.4x the small font (at least 14 px) with a 1 px dark shadow; other overlay labels unchanged.\n- Snapshots `egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png` regenerated (the triad). **They overlap PRs #188, #201, #213** - whichever merges later regenerates them.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#195).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: every binary green (lib 239 passed, 2 ignored; snapshots match). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `law_tests::gizmo_tests::the_origin_triad_is_also_stroked_in_screen_space` (one stroke per axis, none when hidden, a readable Z blue, axis letters told apart)\n- `law_tests::a_fresh_world_shows_only_the_world_axes` and `::a_moved_origin_shows_axes_and_triad_together` (updated for the lighter dimming)\n\nChangelog: The origin triad is drawn chunkier (3 px, outlined) and shorter, with a brighter Z and larger axis letters\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork) - feat, merges at the next cut.\n\nFixes #195\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
